# Report Filter Dropdown Standard

All **Reports** filter dropdowns (including SDV Report) must use the same UI pattern as **Patient Details Report** (`app/reports/export-patient-details/page.jsx`).

## Required pattern

- Use shared classes from `lib/reports/studySitePatientReportUi.js`:
  - `REPORT_SELECT_TRIGGER_CLASS`, `REPORT_SELECT_CONTENT_CLASS`, `REPORT_SELECT_ITEM_CLASS`, `REPORT_SELECT_SEARCH_INPUT_CLASS`
- Use `components/reports/ReportFilterSelect.jsx` for searchable dropdowns (do not invent a new dropdown layout).
- Inside `SelectContent`:
  1. Sticky search row (`p-3 border-b`, magnifier + `Input` with `stopPropagation` on click/keydown)
  2. Scrollable list wrapper: `REPORT_SELECT_SCROLL_LIST_CLASS` (`max-h-[300px] overflow-y-auto`)
  3. Optional first item: `SelectItem value="all"` with label like `All Studies` / `All Sites` (not `Select Study` as a list row)
- Study display names: `getStudyFilterDisplayName()` (protocol / name / fallback `Study {id}`)

## Do not

- Put `SelectItem` rows directly under `SelectContent` without the scroll wrapper
- Use a different border, padding, or search-in-dropdown layout on one report only
- Replace the standard Select with native `<select>` or custom popovers unless explicitly approved

## Reference

- Canonical implementation: `app/reports/export-patient-details/page.jsx` (Study + Site filters)
- Shared component: `components/reports/ReportFilterSelect.jsx`
- SDV Report filters: `components/reports/SdvReportFilters.jsx`
- SDV Report page shell + results table: same as Audit Log (`REPORT_CARD_CLASS`, `REPORT_RESULTS_HEADER_CLASS`, `REPORT_TABLE_TH_CLASS` in `studySitePatientReportUi.js`)
